</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_decrypt;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;935;13;942;;;;vpos;;v;;astring|bool;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data: Decryption&#10;Algorithm:&#10;XChaCha20-Poly1305&#10;This mode uses a 64-bit random nonce with a 64-bit counter.&#10;IETF mode uses a 96-bit random nonce with a 32-bit counter.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$ciphertext&lt;/b&gt;: Encrypted message (with Poly1305 MAC appended)&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$assocData&lt;/b&gt;: Authenticated Associated Data (unencrypted)&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$nonce&lt;/b&gt;: Number to be used only Once;s must be 8 bytes&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$key&lt;/b&gt;: Encryption key&#10;    bool &lt;b&gt;$dontFallback&lt;/b&gt;: Don&apos;t fallback to ext/sodium&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;           The original plaintext message;;d-1,-1;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $ciphertext;;p $assocData;;p $nonce;;p $key;;p $dontFallback;;p;;x;;x;;x;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_encrypt;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;992;5;1025;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_encrypt(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $plaintext = &apos;&apos;,&#10;        string $assocData = &apos;&apos;,&#10;        string $nonce = &apos;&apos;,&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $key = &apos;&apos;,&#10;        bool $dontFallback = false&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data&#10;Algorithm:&#10;XChaCha20-Poly1305&#10;This mode uses a 64-bit random nonce with a 64-bit counter.&#10;IETF mode uses a 96-bit random nonce with a 32-bit counter.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$plaintext&lt;/b&gt;: Message to be encrypted&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$assocData&lt;/b&gt;: Authenticated Associated Data (unencrypted)&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$nonce&lt;/b&gt;: Number to be used only Once;s must be 8 bytes&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$key&lt;/b&gt;: Encryption key&#10;    bool &lt;b&gt;$dontFallback&lt;/b&gt;: Don&apos;t fallback to ext/sodium&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   Ciphertext with a 16-byte Poly1305 message authentication code appended;;d14,1000;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $plaintext;;p $assocData;;p $nonce;;p $key;;p $dontFallback;;p;;x;;x;;x;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_keygen;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1035;5;1038;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_keygen(): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Return a secure random key for use with the XChaCha20-Poly1305&#10;symmetric AEAD interface.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: Exception&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: Error;;d4,1036;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_auth;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1056;5;1073;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_auth(&#10;        string $message,&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $key&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Authenticate a message. Uses symmetric-key cryptography.&#10;Algorithm:&#10;HMAC-SHA512-256. Which is HMAC-SHA-512 truncated to 256 bits.&#10;Not to be confused with HMAC-SHA-512/256 which would use the&#10;SHA-512/256 hash function (uses different initial parameters&#10;but still truncates to 256 bits to sidestep length-extension&#10;attacks).&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$message&lt;/b&gt;: Message to be authenticated&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$key&lt;/b&gt;: Symmetric authentication key&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   Message authentication code;;d14,1060;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $message;;p $key;;p;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_auth_keygen;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1080;5;1083;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_auth_keygen(): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    &lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: Exception&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: Error;;d4,1081;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_auth_verify;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1096;5;1118;;;;vpos;;v;;abool;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_auth_verify(&#10;        string $mac,&#10;        string $message,&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $key&#10;    ): bool&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Verify the MAC of a message previously authenticated with crypto_auth.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$mac&lt;/b&gt;: Message authentication code&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$message&lt;/b&gt;: Message whose authenticity you are attempting to verify (with a given MAC and key)&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$key&lt;/b&gt;: Symmetric authentication key&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   TRUE if authenticated, FALSE otherwise;;d12,1101;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $mac;;p $message;;p $key;;p;;x;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_box;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1136;5;1158;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_box(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $plaintext,&#10;        string $nonce,&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $keypair&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Authenticated asymmetric-key encryption. Both the sender and recipient&#10;may decrypt messages.&#10;Algorithm: X25519-XSalsa20-Poly1305.&#10;X25519: Elliptic-Curve Diffie Hellman over Curve25519.&#10;XSalsa20: Extended-nonce variant of salsa20.&#10;Poyl1305: Polynomial MAC for one-time message authentication.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$plaintext&lt;/b&gt;: The message to be encrypted&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$nonce&lt;/b&gt;: A Number to only be used Once;s must be 24 bytes&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$keypair&lt;/b&gt;: Your secret key and your recipient&apos;s public key&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   Ciphertext with 16-byte Poly1305 MAC;;d14,1142;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $plaintext;;p $nonce;;p $keypair;;p;;x;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_box_keypair;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1235;5;1244;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_box_keypair(): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Generate a new random X25519 keypair.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   A 64-byte string;s the first 32 are your secret key, while the last 32 are your public key. crypto_box_secretkey() and crypto_box_publickey() exist to separate them so you don&apos;t accidentally get them mixed up!;;d4,1236;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_box_keypair_from_secretkey_and_publickey;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1256;5;1276;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_box_keypair_from_secretkey_and_publickey(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $secretKey,&#10;        string $publicKey&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Combine two keys into a keypair for use in library methods that expect&#10;a keypair. This doesn&apos;t necessarily have to be the same person&apos;s keys.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$secretKey&lt;/b&gt;: Secret key&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$publicKey&lt;/b&gt;: Public key&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   Keypair;;d14,1260;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $secretKey;;p $publicKey;;p;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_box_open;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1288;13;1293;;;;vpos;;v;;astring|bool;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Decrypt a message previously encrypted with crypto_box().&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$ciphertext&lt;/b&gt;: Encrypted message&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$nonce&lt;/b&gt;: Number to only be used Once;s must be 24 bytes&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$keypair&lt;/b&gt;: Your secret key and the sender&apos;s public key&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;         The original plaintext message;;d-1,-1;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $ciphertext;;p $nonce;;p $keypair;;p;;x;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_box_publickey;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1322;5;1338;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_box_publickey(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $keypair&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Extract the public key from a crypto_box keypair.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$keypair&lt;/b&gt;: Keypair containing secret and public key&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   Your crypto_box public key;;d14,1325;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $keypair;;p;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_box_publickey_from_secretkey;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1348;5;1363;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_box_publickey_from_secretkey(&#10;        string $secretKey&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Calculate the X25519 public key from a given X25519 secret key.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$secretKey&lt;/b&gt;: Any X25519 secret key&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   The corresponding X25519 public key;;d14,1350;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $secretKey;;p;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_box_seal;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1176;5;1193;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_box_seal(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $plaintext,&#10;        string $publicKey&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Anonymous public-key encryption. Only the recipient may decrypt messages.&#10;Algorithm: X25519-XSalsa20-Poly1305, as with crypto_box.&#10;The sender&apos;s X25519 keypair is ephemeral.&#10;Nonce is generated from the BLAKE2b hash of both public keys.&#10;This provides ciphertext integrity.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$plaintext&lt;/b&gt;: Message to be sealed&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$publicKey&lt;/b&gt;: Your recipient&apos;s public key&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   Sealed message that only your recipient can decrypt;;d14,1180;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $plaintext;;p $publicKey;;p;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_box_seal_open;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1207;13;1210;;;;vpos;;v;;astring|bool;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Opens a message encrypted with crypto_box_seal(). Requires&#10;the recipient&apos;s keypair (sk || pk) to decrypt successfully.&#10;This validates ciphertext integrity.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$ciphertext&lt;/b&gt;: Sealed message to be opened&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$keypair&lt;/b&gt;: Your crypto_box keypair&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;         The original plaintext message;;d-1,-1;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $ciphertext;;p $keypair;;p;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_box_secretkey;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1373;5;1389;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_box_secretkey(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $keypair&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Extract the secret key from a crypto_box keypair.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$keypair&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   Your crypto_box secret key;;d14,1376;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $keypair;;p;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_box_seed_keypair;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1399;5;1410;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_box_seed_keypair(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $seed&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Generate an X25519 keypair from a seed.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$seed&lt;/b&gt;;;d14,1402;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $seed;;p;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_generichash;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1424;5;1450;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_generichash(&#10;        string $message,&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        ?string $key = &apos;&apos;,&#10;        int $length = self::CRYPTO_GENERICHASH_BYTES&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Calculates a BLAKE2b hash, with an optional key.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$message&lt;/b&gt;: The message to be hashed&#10;    string|null &lt;b&gt;$key&lt;/b&gt;: If specified, must be a string between 16 and 64 bytes long&#10;    int &lt;b&gt;$length&lt;/b&gt;: Output length in bytes;s must be between 16 and 64 (default = 32)&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   Raw binary;;d14,1429;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $message;;p $key;;p $length;;p;;x;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_generichash_final;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1462;5;1488;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_generichash_final(&#10;        string &amp;$ctx,&#10;        int $length = self::CRYPTO_GENERICHASH_BYTES&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Get the final BLAKE2b hash output for a given context.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&lt;b&gt;psalm&lt;/b&gt;: -suppress ReferenceConstraintViolation&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$ctx&lt;/b&gt;: BLAKE2 hashing context. Generated by crypto_generichash_init().&#10;    int &lt;b&gt;$length&lt;/b&gt;: Hash output size.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   Final BLAKE2b hash.;;d14,1465;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $ctx;;p $length;;p;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_generichash_init;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1500;5;1526;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_generichash_init(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        ?string $key = &apos;&apos;,&#10;        int $length = self::CRYPTO_GENERICHASH_BYTES&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Initialize a BLAKE2b hashing context, for use in a streaming interface.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string|null &lt;b&gt;$key&lt;/b&gt;: If specified must be a string between 16 and 64 bytes&#10;    int &lt;b&gt;$length&lt;/b&gt;: The size of the desired hash output&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   A BLAKE2 hashing context, encoded as a string (To be 100% compatible with ext/libsodium);;d14,1504;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $key;;p $length;;p;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_generichash_init_salt_personal;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1540;5;1560;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_generichash_init_salt_personal(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        ?string $key = &apos;&apos;,&#10;        int $length = self::CRYPTO_GENERICHASH_BYTES,&#10;        string $salt = &apos;&apos;,&#10;        string $personal = &apos;&apos;&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Initialize a BLAKE2b hashing context, for use in a streaming interface.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string|null &lt;b&gt;$key&lt;/b&gt;: If specified must be a string between 16 and 64 bytes&#10;    int &lt;b&gt;$length&lt;/b&gt;: The size of the desired hash output&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$salt&lt;/b&gt;: Salt (up to 16 bytes)&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$personal&lt;/b&gt;: Personalization string (up to 16 bytes)&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   A BLAKE2 hashing context, encoded as a string (To be 100% compatible with ext/libsodium);;d14,1546;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $key;;p $length;;p $salt;;p $personal;;p;;x;;xCRYPTO_GENERICHASH_BYTES;;xCRYPTO_GENERICHASH_BYTES;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_generichash_keygen;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1592;5;1595;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_generichash_keygen(): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    &lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: Exception&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: Error;;d4,1593;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_generichash_update;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1573;5;1585;;;;vpos;;v;;avoid;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_generichash_update(string &amp;$ctx, string $message): void&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Update a BLAKE2b hashing context with additional data.&#10;-out string $ctx&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$ctx&lt;/b&gt;: BLAKE2 hashing context. Generated by crypto_generichash_init(). $ctx is passed by reference and gets updated in-place.&#10;    &#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$message&lt;/b&gt;: The message to append to the existing hash state.;;d4,1574;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;lctx;;pmessage;;p;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_kdf_derive_from_key;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1605;5;1636;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_kdf_derive_from_key(&#10;        int $subkey_len,&#10;        int $subkey_id,&#10;        string $context,&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $key&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    &lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    int &lt;b&gt;$subkey_len&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    int &lt;b&gt;$subkey_id&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$context&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$key&lt;/b&gt;;;d14,1611;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $subkey_len;;p $subkey_id;;p $context;;p $key;;p;;x;;x;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_kdf_keygen;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1643;5;1646;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_kdf_keygen(): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    &lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: Exception&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: Error;;d4,1644;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_kx;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1677;5;1724;;;;vpos;;v;;astring;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_kx(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $my_secret,&#10;        string $their_public,&#10;        string $client_public,&#10;        string $server_public,&#10;        bool $dontFallback = false&#10;    ): string&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Perform a key exchange, between a designated client and a server.&#10;Typically, you would designate one machine to be the client and the&#10;other to be the server. The first two keys are what you&apos;d expect for&#10;scalarmult() below, but the latter two public keys don&apos;t swap places.&#10;| ALICE                          | BOB                                 |&#10;| Client                         | Server                              |&#10;|--------------------------------|-------------------------------------|&#10;| shared = crypto_kx(            | shared = crypto_kx(                 |&#10;|     alice_sk,                  |     bob_sk,                         | &lt;- contextual&#10;|     bob_pk,                    |     alice_pk,                       | &lt;- contextual&#10;|     alice_pk,                  |     alice_pk,                       | &lt;----- static&#10;|     bob_pk                     |     bob_pk                          | &lt;----- static&#10;| )                              | )                                   |&#10;They are used along with the scalarmult product to generate a 256-bit&#10;BLAKE2b hash unique to the client and server keys.&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: TypeError&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$my_secret&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$their_public&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$client_public&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$server_public&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    bool &lt;b&gt;$dontFallback&lt;/b&gt;;;d14,1684;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $my_secret;;p $their_public;;p $client_public;;p $server_public;;p $dontFallback;;p;;x;;x;;x;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="crypto_kx_client_session_keys;PHP:Function Name;3117689904;f18;1761;5;1792;;;;vpos;;v;;aarray;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    crypto_kx_client_session_keys(&#10;        #[SensitiveParameter]&#10;        string $keypair,&#10;        string $serverPublicKey&#10;    ): array&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    &lt;b&gt;throws&lt;/b&gt;: SodiumException&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$keypair&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$serverPublicKey&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   {0: string, 1: string};;d13,1765;;b1,5;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l $keypair;;p $serverPublicKey;;p;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
