<treenode node="LegacyException;TS:Interface Name;2945743116;f7;9;1;54;;;;vpos;;v;;aError;;c;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    interface LegacyException extends Error&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    The exception type thrown by {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: renderSync and passed as the error to&#10;{&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: render&apos;s callback.&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: Legacy&#10;&lt;b&gt;deprecated&lt;/b&gt;: This is only thrown by the legacy &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: render and &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;&#10;renderSync} APIs. Use {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: compile, &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: compileString, &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;&#10;compileAsync}, and {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: compileStringAsync instead.;;d47,9;;b0,0;;m0;;e1;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
<treenode node="column;JS:JS Var Name;2945743116;f0;35;8;35;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    The (1-based) column number within {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: line at which the error&#10;occurred, if this exception is associated with a specific Sass file&#10;location.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="file;JS:JS Var Name;2945743116;f0;53;6;53;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    If this exception was caused by an error in a Sass file, this will&#10;represent the Sass file&apos;s location. It can be in one of three formats:&#10;* If the Sass file was loaded from disk, this is the path to that file.&#10;* If the Sass file was generated by an importer, this is its canonical URL.&#10;* If the Sass file was passed as {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: LegacyStringOptions.data without a&#10;corresponding {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: LegacyStringOptions.file, this is the special&#10;string `&quot;stdin&quot;`.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="formatted;JS:JS Var Name;2945743116;f0;22;11;22;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    The error message. For Dart Sass, this is the same as the result of calling&#10;{&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: toString, which is itself the same as &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: message but with the&#10;prefix &quot;Error:&quot;.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="message;JS:JS Var Name;2945743116;f0;15;9;15;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    The error message. For Dart Sass, when possible this includes a highlighted&#10;indication of where in the source file the error occurred as well as the&#10;Sass stack trace.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="status;JS:JS Var Name;2945743116;f0;41;8;41;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Analogous to the exit code for an executable. `1` for an error caused by a&#10;Sass file, `3` for any other type of error.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
</treenode>
<treenode node="LegacyException;JS:JS Var Export;3403593292;f8;83;23;83;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e1;;i0;;o\legacy\exception.ts;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="LegacyFileOptions;TS:Interface Name;1181735955;f7;579;1;614;;;;vpossync;;v;;aLegacySharedOptions;;c;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    interface LegacyFileOptions&lt;sync extends &apos;sync&apos; | &apos;async&apos;&gt;&#10;  extends LegacySharedOptions&lt;sync&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    If {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: file is passed without &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: data, Sass will load the stylesheet&#10;at {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: file and compile it to CSS.&#10;&lt;b&gt;typeParam&lt;/b&gt;: sync - This lets the TypeScript checker verify that &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;&#10;LegacyAsyncImporter}s and {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: LegacyAsyncFunctions aren&apos;t passed to&#10;{&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: renderSync.;;d36,580;;b0,0;;m0;;e1;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
<treenode node="data;JS:JS Var Name;1181735955;f0;613;6;613;;;;vposnever;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    See {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: LegacyStringOptions.file for documentation of passing &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;&#10;file} along with {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: data.&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: Input;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="file;JS:JS Var Name;1181735955;f0;605;6;605;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    The path to the file for Sass to load and compile. If the file’s extension&#10;is `.scss`, it will be parsed as SCSS;s if it’s `.sass`, it will be parsed&#10;as the indented syntax;s and if it’s `.css`, it will be parsed as plain CSS.&#10;If it has no extension, it will be parsed as SCSS.&#10;&lt;b&gt;example&lt;/b&gt;&#10;```js&#10;sass.renderSync({file: &quot;style.scss&quot;});s&#10;```&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: Input&#10;&lt;b&gt;compatibility&lt;/b&gt;: feature: &quot;Plain CSS files&quot;, dart: &quot;1.11.0&quot;, node: &quot;partial&quot;&#10;Node Sass and older versions of Dart Sass support loading files with the&#10;extension `.css`, but contrary to the specification they’re treated as SCSS&#10;files rather than being parsed as CSS. This behavior has been deprecated&#10;and should not be relied on. Any files that use Sass features should use&#10;the `.scss` extension.&#10;All versions of Node Sass and Dart Sass otherwise support the file option&#10;as described below.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
</treenode>
<treenode node="LegacyFileOptions;JS:JS Var Export;3403593292;f0;104;19;104;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e1;;i0;;o\legacy\options.ts;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
