<treenode node="importers;JS:Function Name;600094962;f0;246;11;246;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Custom importers that control how Sass resolves loads from rules like&#10;[`&#10;&lt;b&gt;use&lt;/b&gt;: `](https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/use) and&#10;[`&#10;&lt;b&gt;import&lt;/b&gt;: `](https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/import).&#10;Loads are resolved by trying, in order:&#10;- The importer that was used to load the current stylesheet, with the&#10;loaded URL resolved relative to the current stylesheet&apos;s canonical URL.&#10;- Each {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: Importer, &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: FileImporter, or&#10;{&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: NodePackageImporter in &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: importers, in order.&#10;- Each load path in {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: loadPaths, in order.&#10;If none of these return a Sass file, the load fails and Sass throws an&#10;error.&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: Plugins;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;lImporter;;psync;;pFileImporter;;psync;;pNodePackageImporter;;p;;x;;x;;x;;x;;x;;n">
