</treenode>
<treenode node="jsxRuntime;JS:JS Var Name;1533706606;f0;28;14;28;;;;vposString;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Transformation mode for the JSX transform.&#10;- &quot;classic&quot; refers to the original behavior using `React.createElement`.&#10;- &quot;automatic&quot; refers to the transform behavior released with React 17,&#10;where the `jsx` function (or a variation) is automatically imported.&#10;- &quot;preserve&quot; leaves the JSX as-is.&#10;Default value: &quot;classic&quot;.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="keepUnusedImports;JS:JS Var Name;1533706606;f0;54;21;54;;;;vposboolean;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    If specified, disable automatic removal of type-only import and export&#10;statements and names. Only statements and names that explicitly use the&#10;`type` keyword are removed.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="loadPaths;JS:JS Var Name;600094962;f0;267;11;267;;;;vposArray;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Paths in which to look for stylesheets loaded by rules like&#10;[`&#10;&lt;b&gt;use&lt;/b&gt;: `](https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/use) and&#10;[`&#10;&lt;b&gt;import&lt;/b&gt;: `](https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/import).&#10;A load path `loadPath` is equivalent to the following {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: FileImporter:&#10;```js&#10;{&#10;findFileUrl(url) {&#10;// Load paths only support relative URLs.&#10;if (/^[a-z]+:/i.test(url)) return null;s&#10;return new URL(url, pathToFileURL(loadPath));s&#10;}&#10;}&#10;```&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: Input;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="loaders;JS:JS Var Name;61843596;f0;24;8;24;;;;vposLoaders;;v;;a;;r;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="logger;JS:JS Var Name;600094962;f0;281;8;281;;;;vposLogger;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    An object to use to handle warnings and/or debug messages from Sass.&#10;By default, Sass emits warnings and debug messages to standard error, but&#10;if {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: Logger.warn or &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: Logger.debug is set, this will invoke&#10;them instead.&#10;The special value {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: Logger.silent can be used to easily silence all&#10;messages.&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: Messages;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
