</treenode>
<treenode node="quietDeps;JS:JS Var Name;600094962;f0;302;11;302;;;;vposboolean;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    If this option is set to `true`, Sass won’t print warnings that are caused&#10;by dependencies. A “dependency” is defined as any file that’s loaded&#10;through {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: loadPaths or &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: importers. Stylesheets that are&#10;imported relative to the entrypoint are not considered dependencies.&#10;This is useful for silencing deprecation warnings that you can’t fix on&#10;your own. However, please &lt;em&gt;also&lt;/em&gt; notify your dependencies of the deprecations&#10;so that they can get fixed as soon as possible!&#10;**Heads up!** If {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: compileString or &#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: compileStringAsync is&#10;called without {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: StringOptions.url, &lt;em&gt;all&lt;/em&gt; stylesheets it loads&#10;will be considered dependencies. Since it doesn’t have a path of its own,&#10;everything it loads is coming from a load path rather than a relative&#10;import.&#10;&lt;b&gt;defaultValue&lt;/b&gt;: `false`&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: Messages;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="readable;JS:JS Var Name;2838787410;f0;23;10;23;;;;vposboolean;;v;;a;;r;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="silenceDeprecations;JS:JS Var Name;600094962;f0;316;21;316;;;;vposArray;;vDeprecationOrId;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    A set of active deprecations to ignore.&#10;If a deprecation warning of any provided type is encountered during&#10;compilation, the compiler will ignore it instead.&#10;**Heads up!** The deprecated functionality you&apos;re depending on will&#10;eventually break.&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: Messages&#10;&lt;b&gt;compatiblity&lt;/b&gt;: dart: &quot;1.74.0&quot;, node: false;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="sourceMap;JS:JS Var Name;600094962;f0;330;11;330;;;;vposboolean;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Whether or not Sass should generate a source map. If it does, the source&#10;map will be available as {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: CompileResult.sourceMap.&#10;**Heads up!** Sass doesn&apos;t automatically add a `sourceMappingURL` comment&#10;to the generated CSS. It&apos;s up to callers to do that, since callers have&#10;full knowledge of where the CSS and the source map will exist in relation&#10;to one another and how they&apos;ll be served to the browser.&#10;&lt;b&gt;defaultValue&lt;/b&gt;: `false`&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: Output;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="sourceMapIncludeSources;JS:JS Var Name;600094962;f0;340;25;340;;;;vposboolean;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Whether Sass should include the sources in the generated source map.&#10;This option has no effect if {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: sourceMap is `false`.&#10;&lt;b&gt;defaultValue&lt;/b&gt;: `false`&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: Output;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="sourceMapOptions;JS:JS Var Name;1533706606;f0;83;20;83;;;;vposSourceMapOptions;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    If specified, we also return a RawSourceMap object alongside the code.&#10;filePath must be specified if this option is enabled.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
