</treenode>
<treenode node="include;JS:JS Var Name;38858981;f0;2080;9;2080;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Files to include in this plugin (default all).&#10;&lt;b&gt;default&lt;/b&gt;: [];;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="warnOnError;JS:JS Var Name;38858981;f0;2090;13;2090;;;;vposboolean;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    By default, the plugin quits the build process when it encounters an error. If you set this option to true, it will throw a warning instead and leave the code untouched.&#10;&lt;b&gt;default&lt;/b&gt;: false;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
</treenode>
