</treenode>
<treenode node="useFsEvents;JS:JS Var Name;38858981;f0;212;13;212;;926152582;f0;126;13;126;;;;vposboolean;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Whether to use the `fsevents` watching interface if available. When set to `true` explicitly&#10;and `fsevents` is available this supersedes the `usePolling` setting. When set to `false` on&#10;OS X, `usePolling: true` becomes the default.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="usePolling;JS:JS Var Name;38858981;f0;205;12;205;;926152582;f0;119;12;119;;;;vposboolean;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Whether to use fs.watchFile (backed by polling), or fs.watch. If polling leads to high CPU&#10;utilization, consider setting this to `false`. It is typically necessary to **set this to&#10;`true` to successfully watch files over a network**, and it may be necessary to successfully&#10;watch files in other non-standard situations. Setting to `true` explicitly on OS X overrides&#10;the `useFsEvents` default.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
