<treenode node="getIn;JS:Function Name;4218074545;f0;4437;9;4437;;;;vpos;;v;;aunknown;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Returns the value found by following a path of keys or indices through&#10;nested Collections.&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate --&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const { Map, List } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;)&#10;const deepData = Map({ x: List([ Map({ y: 123 }) ]) });s&#10;deepData.getIn([&apos;x&apos;, 0, &apos;y&apos;]) // 123&#10;```&#10;Plain JavaScript Object or Arrays may be nested within an Immutable.js&#10;Collection, and getIn() can access those values as well:&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate --&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const { Map, List } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;)&#10;const deepData = Map({ x: [ { y: 123 } ] });s&#10;deepData.getIn([&apos;x&apos;, 0, &apos;y&apos;]) // 123&#10;```;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;lsearchKeyPath;;punknown;;pnotSetValue;;pIterable;;x;;xoptional unknown;;x;;n">
