<treenode node="hashCode;JS:Function Name;4218074545;f0;4367;12;4367;;;;vpos;;v;;anumber;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Computes and returns the hashed identity for this Collection.&#10;The `hashCode` of a Collection is used to determine potential equality,&#10;and is used when adding this to a `Set` or as a key in a `Map`, enabling&#10;lookup via a different instance.&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate&#10;{ &quot;preamble&quot;: &quot;const { Set,  List } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;)&quot; }&#10;--&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const a = List([ 1, 2, 3 ]);s&#10;const b = List([ 1, 2, 3 ]);s&#10;assert.notStrictEqual(a, b);s // different instances&#10;const set = Set([ a ]);s&#10;assert.equal(set.has(b), true);s&#10;```&#10;If two values have the same `hashCode`, they are [not guaranteed&#10;to be equal][Hash Collision]. If two values have different `hashCode`s,&#10;they must not be equal.&#10;[Hash Collision]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collision_(computer_science);;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
