<treenode node="max;JS:Function Name;4218074545;f0;5205;7;5205;;;;vpos;;v;;aV;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Returns the maximum value in this collection. If any values are&#10;comparatively equivalent, the first one found will be returned.&#10;The `comparator` is used in the same way as `Collection#sort`. If it is not&#10;provided, the default comparator is `&gt;`.&#10;When two values are considered equivalent, the first encountered will be&#10;returned. Otherwise, `max` will operate independent of the order of input&#10;as long as the comparator is commutative. The default comparator `&gt;` is&#10;commutative *only* when types do not differ.&#10;If `comparator` returns 0 and either value is NaN, undefined, or null,&#10;that value will be returned.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;lcomparator;;pV;;poptional Comparator;;x;;x;;n">
