<treenode node="sort;JS:Function Name;4218074545;f0;4782;8;4782;;;;vpos;;v;;athis;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Returns a new Collection of the same type which includes the same entries,&#10;stably sorted by using a `comparator`.&#10;If a `comparator` is not provided, a default comparator uses `&lt;` and `&gt;`.&#10;`comparator(valueA, valueB)`:&#10;* Returns `0` if the elements should not be swapped.&#10;* Returns `-1` (or any negative number) if `valueA` comes before `valueB`&#10;* Returns `1` (or any positive number) if `valueA` comes after `valueB`&#10;* Alternatively, can return a value of the `PairSorting` enum type&#10;* Is pure, i.e. it must always return the same value for the same pair&#10;of values.&#10;When sorting collections which have no defined order, their ordered&#10;equivalents will be returned. e.g. `map.sort()` returns OrderedMap.&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate --&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const { Map } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;)&#10;Map({ &quot;c&quot;: 3, &quot;a&quot;: 1, &quot;b&quot;: 2 }).sort((a, b) =&gt; {&#10;if (a &lt; b) { return -1;s }&#10;if (a &gt; b) { return 1;s }&#10;if (a === b) { return 0;s }&#10;});s&#10;// OrderedMap { &quot;a&quot;: 1, &quot;b&quot;: 2, &quot;c&quot;: 3 }&#10;```&#10;Note: `sort()` Always returns a new instance, even if the original was&#10;already sorted.&#10;Note: This is always an eager operation.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;lcomparator;;pV;;poptional Comparator;;x;;x;;n">
</treenode>
