</treenode>
<treenode node="last;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;4411;8;4411;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    In case the `Collection` is not empty returns the last element of the&#10;`Collection`.&#10;In case the `Collection` is empty returns the optional default&#10;value if provided, if no default value is provided returns undefined.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="map;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;4675;7;4675;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Returns a new Collection of the same type with values passed through a&#10;`mapper` function.&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate --&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const { Collection } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;)&#10;Collection({ a: 1, b: 2 }).map(x =&gt; 10 * x)&#10;// Seq { &quot;a&quot;: 10, &quot;b&quot;: 20 }&#10;```&#10;Note: `map()` always returns a new instance, even if it produced the same&#10;value at every step.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="maxBy;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;5222;9;5222;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Like `max`, but also accepts a `comparatorValueMapper` which allows for&#10;comparing by more sophisticated means:&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate --&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const { List, } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;);s&#10;const l = List([&#10;{ name: &apos;Bob&apos;, avgHit: 1 },&#10;{ name: &apos;Max&apos;, avgHit: 3 },&#10;{ name: &apos;Lili&apos;, avgHit: 2 } ,&#10;]);s&#10;l.maxBy(i =&gt; i.avgHit);s // will output { name: &apos;Max&apos;, avgHit: 3 }&#10;```;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="minBy;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;5259;9;5259;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Like `min`, but also accepts a `comparatorValueMapper` which allows for&#10;comparing by more sophisticated means:&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate --&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const { List, } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;);s&#10;const l = List([&#10;{ name: &apos;Bob&apos;, avgHit: 1 },&#10;{ name: &apos;Max&apos;, avgHit: 3 },&#10;{ name: &apos;Lili&apos;, avgHit: 2 } ,&#10;]);s&#10;l.minBy(i =&gt; i.avgHit);s // will output { name: &apos;Bob&apos;, avgHit: 1 }&#10;```;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
