</treenode>
<treenode node="partition;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;4734;13;4734;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Returns a new Collection with the values for which the `predicate`&#10;function returns false and another for which is returns true.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="reduce;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;5038;10;5038;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Reduces the Collection to a value by calling the `reducer` for every entry&#10;in the Collection and passing along the reduced value.&#10;If `initialReduction` is not provided, the first item in the&#10;Collection will be used.&#10;&lt;b&gt;see&lt;/b&gt;: `Array#reduce`.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="reduceRight;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;5053;15;5053;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Reduces the Collection in reverse (from the right side).&#10;Note: Similar to this.reverse().reduce(), and provided for parity&#10;with `Array#reduceRight`.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="sortBy;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;4805;10;4805;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Like `sort`, but also accepts a `comparatorValueMapper` which allows for&#10;sorting by more sophisticated means:&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate --&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const { Map } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;)&#10;const beattles = Map({&#10;John: { name: &quot;Lennon&quot; },&#10;Paul: { name: &quot;McCartney&quot; },&#10;George: { name: &quot;Harrison&quot; },&#10;Ringo: { name: &quot;Starr&quot; },&#10;});s&#10;beattles.sortBy(member =&gt; member.name);s&#10;```&#10;Note: `sortBy()` Always returns a new instance, even if the original was&#10;already sorted.&#10;Note: This is always an eager operation.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
