<treenode node="insert;JS:Function Name;4218074545;f0;336;10;336;;;;vpos;;v;;aList;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Returns a new List with `value` at `index` with a size 1 more than this&#10;List. Values at indices above `index` are shifted over by 1.&#10;This is synonymous with `list.splice(index, 0, value)`.&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate&#10;{ &quot;preamble&quot;: &quot;const { List } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;);s&quot; }&#10;--&gt;&#10;```js&#10;List([ 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 ]).insert(6, 5)&#10;// List [ 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 ]&#10;```&#10;Since `insert()` re-indexes values, it produces a complete copy, which&#10;has `O(N)` complexity.&#10;Note: `insert` *cannot* be used in `withMutations`.;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;lvalue;;pT;;x;;n">
</treenode>
