<treenode node="zip;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;693;7;693;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Returns a List &quot;zipped&quot; with the provided collection.&#10;Like `zipWith`, but using the default `zipper`: creating an `Array`.&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate&#10;{ &quot;preamble&quot;: &quot;const { List } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;);s&quot; }&#10;--&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const a = List([ 1, 2, 3 ]);s&#10;const b = List([ 4, 5, 6 ]);s&#10;const c = a.zip(b);s // List [ [ 1, 4 ], [ 2, 5 ], [ 3, 6 ] ]&#10;```;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="zipAll;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;719;10;719;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Returns a List &quot;zipped&quot; with the provided collections.&#10;Unlike `zip`, `zipAll` continues zipping until the longest collection is&#10;exhausted. Missing values from shorter collections are filled with `undefined`.&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate&#10;{ &quot;preamble&quot;: &quot;const { List } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;);s&quot; }&#10;--&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const a = List([ 1, 2 ]);s&#10;const b = List([ 3, 4, 5 ]);s&#10;const c = a.zipAll(b);s // List [ [ 1, 3 ], [ 2, 4 ], [ undefined, 5 ] ]&#10;```&#10;Note: Since zipAll will return a collection as large as the largest&#10;input, some results may contain undefined values. TypeScript cannot&#10;account for these without cases (as of v2.5).;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
<treenode node="zipWith;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;740;11;740;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Returns a List &quot;zipped&quot; with the provided collections by using a&#10;custom `zipper` function.&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate&#10;{ &quot;preamble&quot;: &quot;const { List } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;);s&quot; }&#10;--&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const a = List([ 1, 2, 3 ]);s&#10;const b = List([ 4, 5, 6 ]);s&#10;const c = a.zipWith((a, b) =&gt; a + b, b);s&#10;// List [ 5, 7, 9 ]&#10;```;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
