<treenode node="merge;JS:JS Var Name;4218074545;f0;1140;9;1140;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Returns a new Map resulting from merging the provided Collections&#10;(or JS objects) into this Map. In other words, this takes each entry of&#10;each collection and sets it on this Map.&#10;Note: Values provided to `merge` are shallowly converted before being&#10;merged. No nested values are altered.&#10;&lt;!-- runkit:activate --&gt;&#10;```js&#10;const { Map } = require(&apos;immutable&apos;)&#10;const one = Map({ a: 10, b: 20, c: 30 })&#10;const two = Map({ b: 40, a: 50, d: 60 })&#10;one.merge(two) // Map { &quot;a&quot;: 50, &quot;b&quot;: 40, &quot;c&quot;: 30, &quot;d&quot;: 60 }&#10;two.merge(one) // Map { &quot;b&quot;: 20, &quot;a&quot;: 10, &quot;d&quot;: 60, &quot;c&quot;: 30 }&#10;```&#10;Note: `merge` can be used in `withMutations`.&#10;&lt;b&gt;alias&lt;/b&gt;: concat;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
