<treenode node="Collection;JS:Function Name;4218074545;f0;4322;21;4322;;;;vposunknown;;v;;aCollection;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Creates a Collection.&#10;The type of Collection created is based on the input.&#10;* If an `Collection`, that same `Collection`.&#10;* If an Array-like, an `Collection.Indexed`.&#10;* If an Object with an Iterator defined, an `Collection.Indexed`.&#10;* If an Object, an `Collection.Keyed`.&#10;This methods forces the conversion of Objects and Strings to Collections.&#10;If you want to ensure that a Collection of one item is returned, use&#10;`Seq.of`.&#10;Note: An Iterator itself will be treated as an object, becoming a `Seq.Keyed`,&#10;which is usually not what you want. You should turn your Iterator Object into&#10;an iterable object by defining a Symbol.iterator (or&#10;@&#10;&lt;b&gt;iterator&lt;/b&gt;: ) method which&#10;returns `this`.&#10;Note: `Collection` is a conversion function and not a class, and does not&#10;use the `new` keyword during construction.;;d-1,-1;;b0,3;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
</treenode>
