<treenode node="Socket;JS:Class Name;377325552;f15;477;1;480;;1598980308;f0;752;1;763;;1375649489;f15;477;1;480;;1515389909;f15;477;1;480;;78312187;f15;83;1;588;;3261542719;f0;48;12;48;;3058502922;f15;83;1;588;;1557669006;f7;40;1;881;;1753186302;f15;83;1;588;;3810269850;f7;42;1;902;;;;vpos;;v;;aEmitter;;cObject_;;cSocketWithUpgrade;;ccomponent_emitter_1;;c;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    class Socket extends SocketWithUpgrade&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    This class provides a WebSocket-like interface to connect to an Engine.IO server. The connection will be established&#10;with one of the available low-level transports, like HTTP long-polling, WebSocket or WebTransport.&#10;This class comes with an upgrade mechanism, which means that once the connection is established with the first&#10;low-level transport, it will try to upgrade to a better transport.&#10;&lt;b&gt;example&lt;/b&gt;&#10;import { Socket } from &quot;engine.io-client&quot;;s&#10;const socket = new Socket();s&#10;socket.on(&quot;open&quot;, () =&gt; {&#10;socket.send(&quot;hello&quot;);s&#10;});s&#10;&lt;b&gt;see&lt;/b&gt;: SocketWithoutUpgrade&#10;&lt;b&gt;see&lt;/b&gt;: SocketWithUpgrade;;d54,477;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;luri;;popts;;popts;;pSocketOptions;;xoptional SocketOptions;;x;;x;;n">
