<treenode node="disconnect;JS:Function Name;78312187;f0;439;14;439;;3058502922;f0;439;14;439;;1557669006;f0;649;5;660;;1753186302;f0;439;14;439;;3810269850;f0;669;5;681;;;;vpos;;v;;aObject_;;cthis;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Disconnects the socket manually. In that case, the socket will not try to reconnect.&#10;If this is the last active Socket instance of the {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: Manager, the low-level connection will be closed.&#10;&lt;b&gt;example&lt;/b&gt;&#10;const socket = io();s&#10;socket.on(&quot;disconnect&quot;, (reason) =&gt; {&#10;// console.log(reason);s prints &quot;io client disconnect&quot;&#10;});s&#10;socket.disconnect();s&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   self;;d-1,-1;;b0,0;;m0;;e0;;i0;;o;;k;;l;;n">
